/* ==========================================================================================
    page strcutre
========================================================================================== */

/index.html        → content (Netflix style)
/workspace.html    → .md learning view
/snippets.html     → submission form
/about.html        → about + manual
/css/style.css     → your custom styles

1. Add :root tokens
2. Add .page-shell-wide and .page-shell-content
3. Add .layout-reading / standard / wide
4. Apply page-shell-content to about/snippets/content pages
5. Apply page-shell-wide to homepage/workspace
6. Remove old random margins/padding per page

/* ==========================================================================================
    Foundation
========================================================================================== */


# Global CSS foundation:

The correct mental model:

1. Bootstrap = foundation (structure)

grid (container, row, col)
layout
responsive behaviour
basic components (nav, cards, forms)

2. Your CSS = design layer (on top)

colours
spacing tweaks
branding
custom UI (glass nav, sidebar, etc.)

/* ==========================================================================================
    ROOT SETTINGS
========================================================================================== */

:root {
  --color-bg: #0f1117;
  --color-surface: #171b24;
  --color-surface-soft: #202633;

  --color-text: #f5f5f7;
  --color-muted: #a1a1aa;
  --color-link: #0d6efd;

  --radius-sm: 8px;
  --radius-md: 16px;
  --radius-lg: 24px;

  --shadow-soft: 0 20px 60px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);

  --space-sm: 8px;
  --space-md: 16px;
  --space-lg: 32px;
}

Then your base styles:

/* ==========================================================================================
    GLOBAL BASE
========================================================================================== */

body {
  background: var(--color-bg);
  color: var(--color-text);
  font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;
}

a {
  color: var(--color-link);
}

img {
  max-width: 100%;
  display: block;
}

Then use variables everywhere:

.custom-card {
  background: var(--color-surface);
  color: var(--color-text);
  border-radius: var(--radius-md);
  box-shadow: var(--shadow-soft);
}

This means later, instead of changing 50 colours, you change one value in :root.

So your CSS order should be:

1. root variables
2. global/base styles
3. Bootstrap overrides
4. layout sections
5. components
6. page-specific styles
7. media queries

That will make the project feel much more professional.